    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f279776d6c37b2790a28c7a1616a695c9e1170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > is a prime number. Prove that for each <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10af8b3fc779f307fe5c87020e433b00a41801d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" >,</span> there exists an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3f8b726378d5420223c5cb14b10f24b202b187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > such that:<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c797287fec5c14d6056d5a19d170109d2ffb5717.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\left(\\begin{array}{c}n\\\\ \\hline p\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{c}n+k\\\\ \\hline p\\end{array}\\right)\\]\"  width=\"157\" height=\"43\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose that $ p$ is a prime number. Prove that for each $ k$, there exists an $ n$ such that:\r\n\\[ \\left(\\begin{array}{c}n\\\\ \\hline p\\end{array}\\right)\\equal{}\\left(\\begin{array}{c}n\\plus{}k\\\\ \\hline p\\end{array}\\right)\\]",
