   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 1370576,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 250107,
    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/39373ad0f592e0aad414c9aebaf981bb327fffc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ ABCD$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"13\" > is a convex quadrilateral. Let <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8af62c87349b0b4047d92b96ab17ec515ce1ac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ F = AB\\cap CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1c92447e6f127c9349fe464d16642923f7782c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ E = AD\\cap BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"117\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1a100f13618d1ac1c99cc10b66ba358fef53ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ T = AC\\cap BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" >.</span> Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5ea11e545bde1cf7c7dce49aa8e7e31bd354b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ A,B,T,E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" > lie on a circle which intersects with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e809956ebd75268055e33f33539471a869865c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ EF$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > at <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b7d554ea7d9094511c084a2682639363022f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/23293d929381045b3b629c3bdfc5d8d61362dcda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > is midpoint of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c1015b840bca4492903e3615afa5eee7cef242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ AB$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" >,</span> then <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17fff0f57df9f753e03fc9af2d6a37c25681bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ \\angle APM = \\angle BPT$\"  width=\"139\" height=\"13\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose that $ ABCD$ is a convex quadrilateral. Let $ F \\equal{} AB\\cap CD$, $ E \\equal{} AD\\cap BC$ and $ T \\equal{} AC\\cap BD$. Suppose that $ A,B,T,E$ lie on a circle which intersects with $ EF$ at $ P$. Prove that if $ M$ is midpoint of $ AB$, then $ \\angle APM \\equal{} \\angle BPT$.",
    "username": "Omid Hatami",
    "post_number": 1,
