   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 598818,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 106062,
    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "This problem is generalization of <a href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=5918\" class=\"bbcode_url\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>.<br>\nSuppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is a graph and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e46fb925b811d2c16e8fffb84989c86784488621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\subset V(G)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" >.</span> Suppose we have arbitrarily assign real numbers to each element of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that we can assign numbers to each vertex in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/857ffeb742757b9933a9dd1167529a14d815fa5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G\\backslash S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" > that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/b/57b3cb77929cbba51ed5d962378e639c1fe312ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v\\in G\\backslash S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" > number assigned to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"8\" > is average of its neighbors.",
    "post_canonical": "This problem is generalization of [url=http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=5918]this one[/url].\r\nSuppose $G$ is a graph and $S\\subset V(G)$. Suppose we have arbitrarily assign real numbers to each element of $S$. Prove that we can assign numbers to each vertex in $G\\backslash S$ that for each $v\\in G\\backslash S$ number assigned to $v$ is average of its neighbors.",
    "username": "Omid Hatami",
    "post_number": 1,
