   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 22328,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 6448,
    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > is a polynomial with integer coefficients and for every natural <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > we have <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91fcc9f04a101f317d5b8ab406164961b234d876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" >.</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1011d18ab7bbdec0e79a65de1a2d3acfee49cc5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k $\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" > is a sequence that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b1e30c4de354f71dffa82f0eeee799b87d2dc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=1, x_{i+1}=p(x_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" > for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" > is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4a6d41204181432504f1108ded79e4a49e0e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N.$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d7e395d2a6e985dfdb984081f6012851992b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" >",
    "post_canonical": "$p$ is a polynomial with integer coefficients and for every natural $n$ we have $p(n)>n$. $x_k $ is a sequence that: $x_1=1, x_{i+1}=p(x_i)$ for every $N$ one of $x_i$ is divisible by $N.$ Prove that $p(x)=x+1$",
    "username": "Omid Hatami",
